   "concern": "C32",
   "verdict": "raised",
   "quote": "far larger than gap estimates from STM, specific heat and other spectroscopies (~0.25\u20130.35 meV)... strongly suggests the fitted \"gaps\" do not represent the superconducting gap.",
   "fixed_in_v1": false
  },
  {
   "concern": "C7",
   "verdict": "raised",
   "quote": "Because the d-vector differs between B\u2082u and B\u2083u, comparing H\u2225a with H\u2225b on the same junction is the natural experiment for resolving the stated ambiguity.",
   "fixed_in_v1": false
  },
  {
   "concern": "C16",
   "verdict": "raised",
   "quote": "The pressure-inhomogeneity interpretation is implausible... Under Daphne 7373 at \u2264 1.4 GPa, pressure gradients are small, and the resistive transition does not show a corresponding T_c spread.",
   "fixed_in_v1": false
  },
  {
   "concern": "C29",
   "verdict": "partly",
   "quote": "The criterion for a ZABS is a sign change of the relevant gap component under specular reflection kz \u2192 \u2212kz, not the relation between I and... qN",
   "fixed_in_v1": false
  },
  {
   "concern": "C6",
   "verdict": "raised",
   "quote": "UTe\u2082 is a Kondo lattice, and heavy-fermion point contacts frequently show Fano-type zero-bias anomalies from hybridization.",
   "fixed_in_v1": false
  },
  {
   "concern": "C13",
   "verdict": "raised",
   "quote": "A_u is shown only with \u0394x = \u0394y = \u0394z and \u0393 = 0.01 meV... With realistic broadening, the A_u peak splitting would be smeared into a single peak.",
   "fixed_in_v1": false
  },
  {
   "concern": "C27",
   "verdict": "raised",
   "quote": "a ZABS on (001) arises from the sign change of the kz-odd component and does not by itself require bulk nodes... PCS on a single surface cannot establish nodes.",
   "fixed_in_v1": false
  },
  {
   "concern": "C5",
   "verdict": "raised",
   "quote": "Only unitary states (d \u00d7 d* = 0) are treated. This excludes non-unitary or chiral proposals (e.g. B\u2083u + iB\u2082u, Refs. 16 and 24)",
   "fixed_in_v1": false
  },
  {
   "concern": "C33",
   "verdict": "raised",
   "quote": "UTe\u2082 has quasi-2D cylindrical Fermi sheets along c... The quantitative meaning of \u0394z/\u0394x(y) on a sphere does not transfer to the real Fermi surface.",
   "fixed_in_v1": false
  },
  {
   "concern": "C11",
   "verdict": "raised",
   "quote": "Side dips are the textbook signature of critical-current and thermal effects... The same test (field dependence) is not performed at any elevated pressure, where the dips actually appear.",
   "fixed_in_v1": false
  },
  {
   "concern": "C9",
   "verdict": "raised",
   "quote": "reducing \u0393 alone converts a shoulder into side dips and satellites. The emergence of side dips under pressure may therefore be driven by \u0393, not by the \u0394z/\u0394x ratio.",
   "fixed_in_v1": false
  },
  {
   "concern": "C18",
   "verdict": "raised",
   "quote": "Eq. (2) with free weights, gaps, Z and \u0393 per channel (\u22658 parameters) can fit almost any multi-dip spectrum. \"Fits rather well\" carries little evidential weight",
   "fixed_in_v1": false
  },
  {
   "concern": "C26",
   "verdict": "raised",
   "quote": "If SC3 emerges via a second transition below SC2, Landau theory generically gives a coexisting two-component state (B\u2082u + B\u2083u or B\u2082u + iB\u2083u), not a replacement.",
